iOS 26.4 moves the feature to show how much mobile data connected devices have used via Personal Hotspot to a more prominent and easily accessible location.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/01/iOS-26.4-Feature.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="alignnone size-full wp-image-1033519" /><br/>
Now available in Personal Hotspot settings below the "Maximize Compatibility" toggle, the functionality breaks down data usage by device, with non-Apple devices simply showing up as a group of "Other Devices." Total Personal Hotspot Data usage is also displayed.<br/>
<br/>
Previously, the feature was buried in cellular settings. It may be particularly helpful to those with a data limit on their carrier plan.<br/>
<br/>
